      tireType: 'SKU-21', tireCondition: 'New',
      tirePressure: 'Standard pressure', roadSurface: 'Wet Asphalt - 8mm',
      load: 'Driver Only',
      testDescription: 'Test Procedure: (Temporary Spare Wheel – Front Axle) 1. Mount the temporary spare wheel on the FRONT LEFT position; keep the OEM specification tire on the FRONT RIGHT. Both rear wheels remain OEM specification. 2. Set standard placard pressure on the OEM wheels and the specified placard pressure on the temporary spare. Record the rolling-radius mismatch between the two front wheels. 3. Load condition: driver only. 4. Ensure minimum water depth is 8 mm. 5. Accelerate the vehicle to 60 kph and maintain a constant 60 kph through the water pool for the specified test distance. 6. Log AQD output and individual wheel speeds continuously; note any AQD activity before entering and after leaving the pool. 7. Expected Result: Aquaplaning detected inside the pool. The mismatched front-axle rolling radius must neither suppress detection nor cause a false trigger outside the pool.',
      testCaseLink: '', testResult: '', comments: 'Temp spare on Front Left. Record rolling-radius mismatch and wheel-speed offset.',
      feature: 'AQD', activityType: 'Validation', drivetrain: 'ICE',
      waterDepth: '8mm', loadCategory: 'Driver Only', roadSurfaceType: 'Wet Asphalt',
